WEBVTT

00:00.200 --> 00:03.000
An AI agent audits a small site through Toadstone’s MCP server. Real tool calls, real output.

00:03.500 --> 00:08.000
Agent (illustrative): I will audit the practice site with Toadstone. First, what can the server do? — tool: tools/list

00:08.500 --> 00:12.200
Agent (illustrative): Start a small crawl of the practice site, capped at 50 URLs. — tool: start_crawl

00:12.700 --> 00:16.400
Agent (illustrative): Poll until it is done. — tool: crawl_status

00:16.900 --> 00:22.400
Agent (illustrative): Now the errors only. — tool: list_issues

00:22.900 --> 00:26.800
Agent (illustrative): The 404 matters most. What is the missing meta description check? — tool: check_reference

00:27.300 --> 00:31.800
Agent (illustrative): Look at one page, /shop/rakes/. — tool: page_detail

00:32.300 --> 00:37.800
Agent (illustrative): What if I drift off the practice site? Guardrails answer. — tool: start_crawl

00:38.500 --> 00:43.700
Found: 1 broken page, 7 pages without a meta description, 8 without structured data, 1 missing viewport, 1 sitemap error: 18 errors on 9 pages. Toadstone is free, self-hosted and source-available.
